<title>USA: ACNielsen begins trading &quot;regular way&quot;.</title>
<headline>ACNielsen begins trading &quot;regular way&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Conn. 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>ACNielsen Corp said Monday its shares began trading &quot;regular way&quot; on the New York Stock Exchange under the symbol ART.N, following its spinoff from Dun &amp; Bradstreet Corp.</p>
<p>The restructuring was completed last week, leading to the creation of three separate companies that previously were folded into Dun &amp; Bradstreet.</p>
<p>There now are Dun &amp; Bradstreet, ACNielsen and Cognizant Corp.</p>
<p>ACNielsen delivers market research, information and analysis to the consumer products and service industries.</p>
</text>
